---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="The manifesto.md badge" description="What the badge asserts, how to add it, and how a listing becomes claimed." path="/badge/">
  <main id="main" class="wrap">
    <h1>The badge</h1>
    <p class="lede">One shields.io endpoint badge per listing, two states.</p>
    <dl class="facts">
      <dt><code>listed</code></dt><dd>Public and in the directory. Anyone may have added it.</dd>
      <dt><code>claimed</code></dt><dd>A maintainer confirmed the listing: their own pull request, the badge merged into their README, or a yes on the listing issue.</dd>
    </dl>
    <h2>Add it to a README</h2>
    <pre><code>[![manifesto.md](https://img.shields.io/endpoint?url=https://manifesto.md/badge/&lt;slug&gt;.json)](https://manifesto.md/&lt;slug&gt;/)</code></pre>
    <p>The endpoint is static JSON in the shields.io endpoint schema, served from <code>/badge/&lt;slug&gt;.json</code> and cached for an hour. Nothing is tracked.</p>
    <h2>What it is not</h2>
    <p>Not a quality mark, not a conformance claim, not an endorsement. Conformance lives on each specification's own site.</p>
  </main>
</Base>
